<title>FRANCE: French November trade surplus 9.50 bln Ffr.</title>
<headline>French November trade surplus 9.50 bln Ffr.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>France had a seasonally adjusted trade surplus in November of 9.50 billion francs compared with a revised surplus in October of 16.71 billion, provisional customs office data released on Friday showed.</p>
<p>The office had originally reported a surplus in October of 16.94 billion francs.  </p>
<p>Detailed figures, in billions of francs and seasonally adjusted unless otherwise stated, were as follows:</p>
<p>					  Nov	Oct</p>
<p> Trade balance			 9.50   16.71</p>
<p> Trade balance (unadjusted)	8.73   17.04</p>
<p> Imports			     111.79  113.85</p>
<p> Exports			     121.29  130.57</p>
<p> Agri-business balance	     4.75    5.73</p>
<p> Energy balance		     -8.75   -7.67</p>
<p> Industrial/military balance     9.62   14.60</p>
<p> Airbus exports	 2.89  (6 planes)  3.64 (8 planes)</p>
<p> Defence (unadj)		     0.25    0.77</p>
<p> Unadjusted exports		120.43  142.84</p>
<p> Unadjusted imports		111.70  125.80</p>
<p> European Union			4.07    5.92</p>
<p> Germany				 0.34    0.66</p>
<p> Japan				  -1.18   -1.45</p>
<p> United States			-2.52   -1.11</p>
<p>Cumulative figures for the first 11 months of the year were as follows:</p>
<p>				     Jan-Nov 1996     Jan-Nov 1995</p>
<p> Before seasonal adjustment   109.61		89.07</p>
<p> Seasonally adjusted	    111.86		91.07</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
</text>
